WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:24.000
Venue for the Finals  Alcatraz

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.420
I'm sorry, Mokuba.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.960
I'll give your body back.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.880
Noa, what are you going to do?

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.530
I'm going back to my father.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.500
But...!

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:02.660
It was only for a short time, but I was happy to have a real body.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.340
Don't go, Noa!

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.830
I remember what it's like to be human again.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:11.380
Thanks to you, Mokuba.  Thank you.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.380
I have to be strong.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:21.800
Here in the real world, I'll live my life to the fullest for Noa.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:26.390
So I shouldn't keep relying on my brother.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.630
What's wrong, Mokuba?

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.320
It's nothing.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:34.040
We're finally here, Brother!

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.640
Yeah.  It's Gozaburo's disgusting legacy.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:42.870
The center of Kaiba Corporation's military department, Alcatraz.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.840
I built the Duel Tower among its ruins.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.880
That's where we'll hold the finals of the Battle City Tournament.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.910
It's time to end this.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.220
Marik's The Winged Dragon of Ra.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.220
This is The Winged Dragon of Ra!

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:04.760
Yugi's Slifer the Sky Dragon.

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:12.520
And my Obelisk the Tormentor.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:19.080
I will acquire all three cards and rule from top of the Duel Tower!

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.580
Big brother...

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.880
Just wait, Alcatraz!

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.910
The battle will soon begin!

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.320
Brother...

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.060
How's Mai?

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.060
I see.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.000
Mai...

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.600
Marik!  What did you do?

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:48.410
I invited her to walk into the darkness.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.710
She'll wander in loneliness forever and never wake up.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:56.010
Maybe you can save her if you defeat me.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.080
Just wait, Mai.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.250
I promise to defeat Marik and save you.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.540
Brother, please win!

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.860
Leave it to me!

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.110
It's finally starting.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:11.880
The last battle.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:20.800
Since you can no longer duel, you're a mere spectator.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.740
What an easy life.

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:24.610
Marik.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.420
Where's Rishido?

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:27.440
I don't know.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:29.130
Don't play dumb.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.110
I know you hid him.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.620
Even if I knew, I wouldn't tell you.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.620
I knew you'd say that.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:38.990
However...

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:48.500
This belongs to you.

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:53.700
You gave the Millennium Necklace to the Pharaoh.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:05:00.310
So you can no longer see the future or protect yourself from the Millennium Rod.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:05.900
I can easily control your mind and learn Rishido's location.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:09.820
I love how scared you look.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:12.820
I never thought I'd get to see that.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:13.820
But...

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:17.560
I don't have time to play around.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.820
We'll be landing at Alcatraz shortly.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.500
Duelists, come to the deck.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:29.330
Rishido was struck by Ra's anger.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:32.080
He won't wake up so easily.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.370
Actually, he may never wake up.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:41.580
Don't count on Kaiba or Yugi to save him.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:45.680
They'll fall victim to my Ra!

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.760
I'm leaving.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:53.560
After I slaughter the Pharaoh in a duel, I'll take my time in ending Rishido.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:06:02.070
Sister, stay quiet and watch the darkness devour all your hope.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.620
Marik...

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:12.600
Is Bakura really gone?

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:17.320
Yeah.  Bakura lost against Marik in a Shadow Game.

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:22.680
Unless someone defeats the winner, the loser can't return.

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:26.830
Yugi, you were here?

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:29.180
Where's Bakura?

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:31.620
I don't know.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:37.260
I don't care where losers go after they lose a Shadow Game.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:40.420
I wonder where Bakura went.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.850
These duels are creating too many victims.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:45.450
I'm sorry.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:46.850
My other self?

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:51.400
This all started because of my lost memories.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:53.250
It's my fault that Marik hates me.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:07:01.400
And why those connected to the Millennium Items - even those that are not - may fall victim.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.370
No!  It's not your fault!

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.380
Partner...

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:10.440
You're not responsible for memories that you don't remember!

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:14.380
You always try to protect everyone!

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:18.120
And we still may be able to save them.

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:20.350
Don't give up!

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:25.730
You're right.  I can only keep moving forward.

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:30.360
A true duelist wouldn't give up in the middle of a game!

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:31.920
Yeah!

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:34.800
There you are!

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.100
We found you, Yugi.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.040
We're about to reach our destination.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:39.880
Right.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:43.340
Where's Bakura anyway?

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:46.340
He's badly hurt.  I hope he's okay.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:49.550
I'm sure the Millennium Ring has something to do with this.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:53.920
It'll be fine!  I'm sure he'll come back!

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:56.920
Right!  Let's have faith and wait for him.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:57.920
You're right.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:18.170
Duelists, step off the ship!

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:22.780
I allow you to step foot on my creation, on the land I'm proud of!

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:29.640
That's where...

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.650
...the finals will take place.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.560
It looks so big up close!

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:35.730
Yeah.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:41.480
That's where we'll fight and determine who stands atop all duelists!

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:42.660
The Duel Tower!

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.230
Kaiba.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:48.740
Yugi!  I will defeat you and stand at the top of the tower!

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:55.950
Kaiba!  Don't forget me!

00:08:55.950 --> 00:09:02.600
When I beat you, you'll learn that you're the king of the mountain - a mountain of garbage!

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:06.620
You're a duelist that's worth less than scrap.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:09.630
I'll bury you in this debris!

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:10.840
What!

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.370
Stop it, Jonouchi!

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:16.410
I made the semifinals, you know!

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:17.370
Calm down!

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:21.020
That's right!  Settle this in a duel!

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:22.720
Fine!

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:23.920
Let's go!

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:25.060
Follow me.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:33.580
This place excites me.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.490
Don't you agree, your majesty?

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:40.990
Marik!  You punk!

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:42.400
Screech!

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.000
Honda, are you still a monkey?

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:50.500
Hey, Mr. Organizer!

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:54.000
How are you determining the matchups for the semifinals?

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.420
Be patient!

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:58.010
You'll know your fate when you go to the tower!

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:02.530
Your fate is death and defeat.

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:14.770
Duelists, welcome to the Duel Tower.

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:19.770
We'll now begin the Battle City Tournament semifinals.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.910
There's nothing here.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.770
How are you going to duel?

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.000
You'll know soon enough.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:35.260
Each duelist will enter one of four doors and head towards the top of the tower.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.450
Four doors.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:00.940
Please choose one of the four doors.

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:08.940
Do not worry.  Your choice of doors will not affect the duel.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:12.670
Even so, I don't know which to pick.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.570
Yugi, what are you picking?

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:15.950
Any door is fine.

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:18.220
Really?  Well then...

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:21.900
Eeny, meeny, miny, moe-

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:26.190
An indecisive fool should take the one that's left.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:28.200
-and you are it.

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:30.280
Okay!  I'll take that door!

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:34.780
Hey!  I picked that one!

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:36.920
Jonouchi.  I'm going too.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:40.310
H-Hey Yugi!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.310
There's only one left.

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:48.050
We'll go this way.

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:51.780
Jonouchi, maybe they "saved the best for last."

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:53.060
Good luck!

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:59.960
This is a card battle system.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.370
What are we going to do?

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:12.040
We're here!

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:15.540
Wow!  The ceiling is so high!

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:17.960
This is where they're dueling?

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:21.050
But what are the matchups?

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.790
We'll decide that now.

00:12:26.130 --> 00:12:27.630
Jonouchi?

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:33.460
What?

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:35.600
What are you doing, Jonouchi?

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.370
I don't know!

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:39.600
Hey Kaiba!  Explain!

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:41.200
Be quiet and listen!

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:44.390
We'll explain it so easily that even a fool can understand.

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:45.610
Say what!

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:51.200
An event as grand as deciding the true Duel King...

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:56.000
...requires a proper method for choosing the semifinal matchups.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:59.620
You will play a game to determine your opponent!

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.620
A game will determine my opponent?

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:04.400
The rules are simple.

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:07.570
The four duelists will battle simultaneously.

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:11.730
The first two to reach the top will duel in the first semifinals.

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:15.070
The last two will duel in the second semifinals.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:18.070
So it's a 4-person battle royal?

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.070
The game is Duel Monsters, of course.

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:22.950
You'll have 4000 life points.

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:26.400
As you lose life points, you'll rise up.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:30.080
You'll reach the top in order of defeat.

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:35.680
I'll now explain the rules.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:41.830
Each player will use a 40-card deck that they created for this tournament.

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:44.330
Set your decks in your Duel Disks.

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:51.230
By connecting your Duel Disk, each player's cards are displayed on the screen panel.

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:56.000
The four players alternate turns.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:59.230
You can attack any player you want.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:06.340
The first two duelists to lose will fight each other in the first semifinals.

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:09.460
Phew.  That's a load off my mind.

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:13.500
Because even if you lose, you're not out of the tournament.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:18.000
You're wrong.  This is an important duel.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:20.730
What do you mean, Otogi?

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:23.240
It'll be a psychological battle.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:28.740
For example, let's say Jonouchi wants to duel Yugi in the semifinals.

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:33.540
But the other two may support Yugi.

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:38.430
Or all three may focus their attacks on him.

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:39.700
I see.

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:44.120
In a battle royal, it's quicker to get rid of players one-by-one.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:46.980
Who's the most likely target?

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:50.000
What are you looking at?

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:53.730
Try not to lose too quickly!

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:56.740
Be quiet!  Stop saying stuff like that!

00:14:56.970 --> 00:15:01.020
The purpose of this game is to divide us into two groups.

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:05.520
If I use my strategies correctly, I can choose my opponent.

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:09.920
My opponent in the semifinals will be...

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.430
I only have one target.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:16.420
Marik's tremendously powerful Ra card.

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:21.360
In order to defeat him, I need two God Cards.

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:26.430
So my opponent in the semifinals will be the one who has the other God Card.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:28.430
Yugi.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.410
Who'll be my opponent?

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:37.910
Yugi, I'm itching to kill you.

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:46.150
Yugi, I've made it this far in Battle City because my goal is to duel you.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:55.530
Yugi, when I keep winning and become a true duelist, I want you to duel me again.

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:57.920
Okay.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:00.670
Let's duel when that time comes, Jonouchi.

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:02.930
Thank you, Yugi.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.570
Jonouchi, I'll wait for you.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:11.240
I'll hold on to your Red-Eyes until then.

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:17.820
I've never forgotten that promise nor my Red-Eyes.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:21.820
I want to duel you and win.

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:26.830
But I have to beat Marik in order to save Mai.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:29.200
Marik.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:33.660
Are you ready?

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:37.070
We'll now decide the turn order.

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:38.570
How?

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:43.540
Each player selects and shows one monster card.

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:47.300
You'll play in order of attack points, highest going first.

00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:51.680
But those monster cards are removed from your decks.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:57.790
If I want to go first, I have to sacrifice a monster with high attack points.

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:05.700
If I go first, I can target my desired opponent and act before anyone else.

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:07.530
I'll have the advantage.

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:11.500
Which card should I choose?

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.240
The psychological battle has already started.

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:16.740
Show your card!

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:24.300
I got this card via ante.  It means nothing to me.

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:25.750
I'm going first.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:33.260
I'm keeping my cards with high attack points.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:35.520
The order is set!

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.280
Seto Kaiba will go first!

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:42.770
Followed by Marik Ishtar, Yugi Muto and Katsuya Jonouchi!

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:51.840
All I have to do is eliminate the two players that I don't want to duel in the semifinals.

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:53.050
Him...

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:56.400
...and the lame one who's barely a duelist.

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:00.340
I want to duel Yugi.

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:04.740
That's what I desire as a duelist.

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:07.740
But before that, I have to...

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:12.600
Who should I duel?

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.840
My other self, are you confused?

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.300
Partner.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:19.480
Yeah.

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:21.820
To be honest, I'm confused.

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:25.010
I have a reason to duel each of them-

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:28.560
No, I want to duel them!

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:33.090
It says the three God Cards will point to the Pharaoh.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:38.400
So the one who gathers the three God Cards will become the Pharaoh.

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:42.830
He will have the seven Millennium Items and regain the lost memories.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:46.830
In order to regain my memories, my true opponent is Marik!

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:51.340
Let's have a fair fight as true duelists!

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:55.110
My promise to Jonouchi as a duelist!

00:18:55.600 --> 00:19:03.000
You know that we're stepping into God's territory in this final tournament.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:06.770
The three God Cards will choose who is truly the strongest!

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:11.080
I will defeat you and Marik and acquire the God Cards.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:14.200
I will become the world's strongest duelist!

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.770
My battle of destiny against Kaiba!

00:19:17.770 --> 00:19:20.900
I have a reason to duel each of them.

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:24.910
Yeah.  So you should do what you think is best.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:29.410
The one I should duel is...

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:34.840
The battle royal to determine the Battle City semifinal matchups!

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:36.410
Start the game!

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:38.650
I go first!  I draw!

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:40.600
I set a card.

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:43.750
I summon Vorse Raider in attack position!

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:45.660
I end my turn.

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:49.330
Players can't attack on their first turn.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:52.660
But I'll make the first move on my next turn.

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:54.670
My turn.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:55.770
I draw!

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:58.670
I summon Newdoria in defense position!

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:02.670
I end my turn.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:06.910
Its effect is pretty useful.

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:09.310
My turn!  I draw!

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:18.890
My soul as a duelist will pick my opponent!

00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:23.020
I summon Big Shield Gardna in defense position!

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:26.900
I set two cards!

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.650
I end my turn!

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:31.390
My turn!

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:35.450
I have a bad hand.

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:38.310
I can't summon any monsters without tributing.

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:41.810
I set a card and end my turn.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:43.720
My turn!

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:46.060
The ecosystem of battle!

00:20:46.060 --> 00:20:48.120
The food chain of battle!

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:52.860
I'll show you that the weak isn't allowed to touch the lion!

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:56.200
Vorse Raider!  Attack the lame one directly!

00:20:58.960 --> 00:21:02.330
This is bad!  Jonouchi has no monsters to defend with!

00:21:02.330 --> 00:21:03.440
Jonouchi!

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:07.840
Go, Vorse Raider!

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.440
I don't think so!

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:11.420
I flip over my set card!

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:14.110
The Continuous Trap, The Regulation of Tribe!

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:19.820
What?

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:20.950
Yugi!

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:25.960
Due to this trap card, the Monster Type I choose can't attack!

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:29.460
The Type I choose is Beast-Warrior!

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:31.960
Yugi!

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:37.060
As a duelist, I will fulfill the promise I made with my friend!

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:47.080
The battle royal will decide the semifinal matchups.

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:51.320
The four duelists' desires clash with each other.

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:54.360
Yugi wants to fulfill his promise with Jonouchi.

00:21:54.360 --> 00:21:58.520
Jonouchi wants to duel Marik to save Mai.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:02.660
Kaiba wants Yugi's Slifer to prepare for Ra.

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:04.820
Marik is eerily silent.

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:07.880
And the duel takes an unexpected turn!

00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:10.160
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Battle Royal!

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:11.600
Duel, standby!

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:23.090
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:23.090 --> 00:22:32.040
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:37.010
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:37.010 --> 00:22:40.980
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:41.410 --> 00:22:48.950
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:48.950 --> 00:22:52.520
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:57.290
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:57.290 --> 00:23:07.400
And walk it without stopping

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:15.010
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:23.980
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:31.960
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:31.960 --> 00:23:41.800
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
